  "name": "curate-context",
  "description": "Creates, imports, pulls, edits, repairs, or publishes a Knowledge Catalog (KC) context set as Open Knowledge Format (OKF v0.2) markdown under `bundle/` with `kcmd`, for BigQuery, Spanner, BigLake, Cloud SQL, AlloyDB, or Hive Metastore. Load FIRST whenever creating, importing, pulling, editing, repairing, or publishing a context set or OKF bundle/folder, or using `kcmd`, before running `kcmd` (never unscoped `kcmd` from pip/npx or unconfirmed `./kcmd`) or editing files: e.g. \"build a context set from our sales tables and metric doc\", \"update churn in our context set and publish\". Plans first, validates, and publishes only after user approval at both gates, even when told to work autonomously. Keeps the user's OKF folder/structure. If also asked for OSI-G semantic models, ontology canvases, new glossary terms, access changes, or certification, still use it: builds the context set and declines those parts. Never for read-only catalog search or data questions.",
